+
+### ANOMALY-2026-10-25-gogen-c2int8 - a text moved into an int8 aborts code generation
+
+- Status: `fixed` locally in the gogen backends.
+- Discovery date: `2026-10-25`
+- Affected path: `tools/gogen/emit-go.mjs` and `emit-js.mjs`, conversion `c2n` with an int8 target. The frontend already decides that conversion (`numeric(to) && charlike(from)`); the two emitters answered `c2n` for an i and an f only, and the runtimes had `ParseI` / `ParseF` and no int8 form.
+- Reproducer: `DATA lv TYPE int8. lv = '42'.` in a class gogen compiles, or `node tools/gogen/semantics.mjs --class zcl_gogen_t_c2int8` against the fixture before the fix.
+- Actual before fix: the emitter throws `no Go for conversion c2n string->int8` / `no JS for conversion c2n string->int8`, so no program that moves a text into an int8 generates at all. A comparison of an int8 against a text reaches the same conversion, and refuses too.
+- Expected SAP behaviour (SAP's character-like source rules, https://help.sap.com/doc/abapdocu_latest_index_htm/latest/en-US/ABENCONVERSION_TYPE_IBS.html and the int8 page): the text rule already measured for an i (`ZCL_GOGEN_T_C2NUM`), at int8's range - blanks around, one sign, a blank between it and the digits allowed, digits with at most one point, no exponent, blanks only 0, the fraction rounded half away from zero before the range is judged; both endpoints exact; out of range `CX_SY_CONVERSION_OVERFLOW`, other text `CX_SY_CONVERSION_NO_NUMBER`. Documentation-backed, no new A4H measurement.
+- Fix: `abap.ParseI8` (`go/abap/conv.go`) and `ParseI8` (`js/abap.mjs`), the two emitters answering `c2n` for an int8 target. Exactness: the magnitude travels as a `uint64` in Go, so 19 digits never wrap the accumulation and MIN keeps its own magnitude, and as a `BigInt` in JS, so `9007199254740993` and `7205000000000000001` keep their last digit where a `Number( )` would round them.
+- Regression tests: `go/abap/conv_i8_test.go`, `tools/gogen/conv-i8.test.mjs`, and the shared fixture `tools/gogen/testdata/zcl_gogen_t_c2int8.clas.abap` pinned in `semantics.mjs`, which runs both backends and catches both classes by ABAP name.
+- Upstream: none; the local gogen backend.
