+## A text into an int8, 2026-10-25
+
+`c2n` reaches int8 in both backends: `abap.ParseI8` (`go/abap/conv.go`) and
+`ParseI8` (`js/abap.mjs`), the text rule `ZCL_GOGEN_T_C2NUM` measured for an
+i at int8's range. Blanks around the value, one sign (a leading `+` or `-`,
+or a trailing `-`, a blank between it and the digits allowed), digits with at
+most one point, no exponent; blanks only are 0; the fraction rounds half away
+from zero **before** the range is judged, so `9223372036854775807.5` overflows
+and `-9223372036854775807.5` is MIN. Out of range is
+`CX_SY_CONVERSION_OVERFLOW`, anything else `CX_SY_CONVERSION_NO_NUMBER`, and
+the generated program catches both by ABAP name.
+
+Every value inside int8 stays exact, both endpoints included: the magnitude
+travels as a `uint64` in Go (19 digits are the widest it holds, so the
+accumulation never wraps, and MIN keeps its own magnitude) and a `BigInt` in
+JS. `9007199254740993` and `7205000000000000001` keep their last digit where
+a `Number( )` would round them, which is also why the value is formatted out
+of the int8 by the template (`abap.FmtI8` / `String( )`) and not through a
+double.
+
+Documentation-backed (SAP's character-like source rules), no new A4H
+measurement. The rows live three times: `go/abap/conv_i8_test.go`,
+`conv-i8.test.mjs` and the fixture `testdata/zcl_gogen_t_c2int8.clas.abap`
+pinned in `semantics.mjs`, which both emitters run.
